.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-family-has-farmed-the-same-land-for-more-than-70-years-as-a-dairy-hay-farm-and-agritourism-business-nearly-40-acres-can-now-never-be-developed-even-though-the-family-keeps-ownership/articleshow/134374676.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-family-has-farmed-the-same-land-for-more-than-70-years-as-a-dairy-hay-farm-and-agritourism-business-nearly-40-acres-can-now-never-be-developed-even-though-the-family-keeps-ownership/articleshow/134374676.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T01:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134374696,imgsize-1359943.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mill Brook Crossing: Athol daylightes buried stream and rips up parking lot; new wetlands cool downtown]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134382536.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[This month, Athol, Massachusetts, proudly marked the successful completion of Mill Brook Crossing. This innovative project not only restored a vital stream but also established new wetlands right in the heart of downtown. With over 53,000 square feet of pavement transformed, the area now features lush vegetation and trees. The redesign emphasizes natural stormwater management and enhances pedestrian safety, turning a former parking lot into an inviting, climate-resilient community space.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/for-half-a-century-massachusetts-mill-brook-ran-beneath-a-downtown-parking-lot-athol-has-now-uncovered-it-created-12000-sq-ft-of-wetlands-and-turned-53000-sq-ft-of-pavement-into-vegetation/articleshow/134382536.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/for-half-a-century-massachusetts-mill-brook-ran-beneath-a-downtown-parking-lot-athol-has-now-uncovered-it-created-12000-sq-ft-of-wetlands-and-turned-53000-sq-ft-of-pavement-into-vegetation/articleshow/134382536.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T00:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134383361,imgsize-1446808.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Maine removes 60-year-old river barrier to reopen migration route for rare Atlantic salmon]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134383952.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/maine-removed-a-60-year-old-river-barrier-where-only-about-25-wild-adult-atlantic-salmon-return-each-year-a-new-nature-like-fishway-aims-to-reopen-migration-routes/articleshow/134383952.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/maine-removed-a-60-year-old-river-barrier-where-only-about-25-wild-adult-atlantic-salmon-return-each-year-a-new-nature-like-fishway-aims-to-reopen-migration-routes/articleshow/134383952.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-21T23:03:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134384077,imgsize-294926.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Sawyer Tinsley, Florida teen who raised $25K for rescue pets after fostering a kitten saved her from loneliness]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134387398.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-sawyer-tinsley-a-16-year-old-florida-teen-who-used-yard-flamingos-to-raise-25k-for-rescue-pets-after-fostering-a-kitten-saved-her-from-loneliness/articleshow/134387398.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-sawyer-tinsley-a-16-year-old-florida-teen-who-used-yard-flamingos-to-raise-25k-for-rescue-pets-after-fostering-a-kitten-saved-her-from-loneliness/articleshow/134387398.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-21T23:02:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134387764,imgsize-742181.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas man, charged with murder of his wife, escapes to Milan just before trial; Italy delays extradition, seeks formal assurance that there would be no death penlty]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134394822.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-man-charged-with-murder-of-his-wife-escapes-to-milan-just-before-trial-italy-delays-extradition-seeks-formal-assurance-that-there-would-be-no-death-penalty/articleshow/134394822.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-man-charged-with-murder-of-his-wife-escapes-to-milan-just-before-trial-italy-delays-extradition-seeks-formal-assurance-that-there-would-be-no-death-penalty/articleshow/134394822.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-21T22:54:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134394854,imgsize-70768.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2019, a Connecticut home renovation uncovered human remains beneath a basement]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134393947.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Amid basement renovations in Ridgefield, Connecticut, workers uncovered human remains and military artifacts, shedding new light on the 1777 Battle of Ridgefield. Notable finds, such as early 'USA' buttons, highlight a growing sense of national unity among Patriot soldiers. Additionally, emerging evidence suggests that the British ambush was more brutal than previously reimagined, prompting ongoing research into this pivotal historical event.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2019-a-connecticut-home-renovation-uncovered-human-remains-beneath-a-basement-seven-years-later-archaeologists-found-early-usa-buttons-and-evidence-reshaping-the-1777-battle-of-ridgefield/articleshow/134393947.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2019-a-connecticut-home-renovation-uncovered-human-remains-beneath-a-basement-seven-years-later-archaeologists-found-early-usa-buttons-and-evidence-reshaping-the-1777-battle-of-ridgefield/articleshow/134393947.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-21T22:51:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134394811,imgsize-1703962.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pakistan in crisis: PTI to hold Sept 27 stir 'at all costs']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134394418.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Pakistan Tehreek-e-Insaf plans a protest on September 27 for Imran Khan's release. Legal challenges have been filed against the detention of his three sisters. The party insists the demonstrations will proceed despite arrests of its leaders. Authorities state the protest will not be allowed to disrupt the capital city. Imran Khan's son condemned the detentions and called for international intervention.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/pakistan-in-crisis-pti-to-hold-sept-27-stir-at-all-costs-imran-khans-sisters-challenge-detention-orders/articleshow/134394418.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/pakistan-in-crisis-pti-to-hold-sept-27-stir-at-all-costs-imran-khans-sisters-challenge-detention-orders/articleshow/134394418.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-21T22:41:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134394628,imgsize-98792.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A concert bet turned 3 baklava trays into a $20,000-a-month business]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134394190.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Jacob Komarow, famously known as the 'Baklava Guy', turned a simple concert bet into a successful enterprise, Good Baklava. This innovative business now rakes in over twenty thousand dollars each month, thanks to its delicious pastries imported from Turkey. With various locations throughout the city and an online platform, his brand recently gained significant recognition from a New York Times feature.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/he-bought-three-trays-of-baklava-for-a-concert-after-a-friend-bet-he-couldnt-sell-them-the-business-now-averages-just-over-20000-a-month-in-sales/articleshow/134394190.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/he-bought-three-trays-of-baklava-for-a-concert-after-a-friend-bet-he-couldnt-sell-them-the-business-now-averages-just-over-20000-a-month-in-sales/articleshow/134394190.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T00:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134394410,imgsize-142140.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK to introduce special rape and serious sexual offence courts, amid low prosecution rate]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134393885.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[British Prime Minister Andy Burnham announced dedicated courts for sexual offence cases. These new courts aim to expedite convictions and reduce case backlogs significantly.  Specialized training will be provided to court personnel for handling sensitive cases.  Victims will receive a dedicated point of contact throughout the legal process.  This initiative supports the government's commitment to reducing violence against women.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-to-introduce-special-rape-and-serious-sexual-offence-courts-as-prosecution-rates-remain-shamefully-low/articleshow/134393885.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-to-introduce-special-rape-and-serious-sexual-offence-courts-as-prosecution-rates-remain-shamefully-low/articleshow/134393885.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-21T22:07:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134393952,imgsize-55904.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[An 8,000-acre South Carolina forest was bought for conservation after drawing developer interest]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134392746.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a move to prioritize environmental sustainability, Georgetown County officials are backing a substantial acquisition of 4,148 acres in Carvers Bay, which will be transformed into a state forest. Another expansive parcel on Waccamaw Neck is also earmarked for conservation. Officials assert that the benefits of long-term land preservation significantly outweigh the potential revenue from taxes, ensuring the safeguarding of precious natural resources in the region.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-8000-acre-south-carolina-forest-was-bought-for-conservation-after-drawing-developer-interest-the-state-now-plans-to-acquire-4148-acres-for-a-new-carvers-bay-state-forest/articleshow/134392746.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-8000-acre-south-carolina-forest-was-bought-for-conservation-after-drawing-developer-interest-the-state-now-plans-to-acquire-4148-acres-for-a-new-carvers-bay-state-forest/articleshow/134392746.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-21T22:04:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134393888,imgsize-1303302.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[He made a work presentation that morning: Family of Bangladeshi-origin AI scientist seeks probe into Irfan Al-Hussaini's July death in Pao Alto, says something is not adding up]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134392996.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/he-made-a-work-presentation-that-morning-family-of-bangladeshi-origin-ai-scientist-seeks-probe-into-irfan-al-hussainis-july-death-in-palo-alto-says-something-is-not-adding-up/articleshow/134392996.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/he-made-a-work-presentation-that-morning-family-of-bangladeshi-origin-ai-scientist-seeks-probe-into-irfan-al-hussainis-july-death-in-palo-alto-says-something-is-not-adding-up/articleshow/134392996.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-21T21:15:51+05:30</